        <mxCell id="g5mHuEgd7DBy27zgcuWZ-280" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot; face=&quot;Helvetica&quot;&gt;As described in figure 1, the wing geometry is characterized by 9 skin thicknesses (top, side, and bottom skin thickness for each of the 3 spanwise sections) and 9 sandwich thicknesses (analogously defined). Based on this, the Structures subsystem introduces 12 geometry constraints that ensure the sandwich panel dimensions are physically feasible: the sandwich thickness must not exceed the wing box height, and the aluminium skin must remain thinner than the core.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The following constraints are imposed:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot; face=&quot;Helvetica&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot; face=&quot;Helvetica&quot;&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="230" width="480" x="3980" y="459.86" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
